MENT HOSPITALS\n†*198. SHRI GOPAL SHETTY:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether the Government has received proposals from the States regarding\nfinancial assistance for improving the infrastructural and other facilities in their\nrespective Government hospitals;\n(b) if so, the details thereof, during the last three years, State/UT -wise including\nMaharashtra;\n(c) the action taken thereon;\n(d) whether the Government proposes to allocate more funds to the States for this\npurpose during the current Five Year Plan; and\n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI JAGAT PRAKASH NADDA)\n(a)  to (e):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 198* FOR 29TH JULY, 2016\n(a) to (e) Government has received proposals from the states in the form of\nProgramme Implementation Plans (PIPs) for financial assistance under National\nHealth Mission (NHM) to strengthen their healthcare systems including for improving\nthe infrastructural and other facilities in their respective Government hospitals. The\nPIPs submitted b y States/UTs and approvals issued in the form of Records of\nProceedings (RoPs) during the last three years are available in public domain\nhttp://nhm.gov.in/nrhm-in-state/state-program-implementation-plans-pips.html.\nResources are allocated to states based on budgetary allocation made for National\nHealth Mission in the Union Budget. The year 2016 -17 is the last year of the current\nFive Year Plan. As such, additional funds to the states in the current Five Year Plan\nmay be available only if there is enhancement in the budget allocation for NHM at RE\nstage and /or if the states earn incentives based on performance on key health\nindicators and health sector reforms.\n\nStatement Showing the State/UTs wise SPIP Approval & Utilization\nunder Hospital Strengthening (B.