 \n(e) if so, the details thereof, State/UTwise and the reasons therefor along with the \naction taken/being taken by the Government on such complaints so far? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SH. PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a) & (b):   The Government has been monitoring the implementation of the report of the \nAICTE Review Committee which has been submitted in April 2015. Based on these \nrecommendations, the AICTE has been restructured to meet the demands of student \nfraternity and technical institutions by promoting R&D, Vocational Education, Online \nEducation, inclusivity and transparency.  Now, the approval system has become online \nand therefore more efficient and transparent. \n \n(c): The state-wise expenditure for the Research Programs during the last three financial \nyears is at Annexure-I. \n \n(d) & (e):   There have been (9) complaints against officials in AICTE.  These complaints are \nentrusted for examination by a committee head ed by retired Justice of High Court. The \nState-wise list of the complaints against AICTE and action taken thereon is at annexure-II. \n***** \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure as referred to in reply to  Part ( c ) of the Lok Sabha Unstarre\nFunctioning of AICTE\n   2013-14 \nSTATE \n Scheme \nResearch Promotion \nScheme \nResearch Park Quality Improvement \nProgramme \nInnovation Pro\nScheme\nFund \nAllocation  \nExpenditur\ne  \nFund \nAllocatio\nn  \nExpenditur\ne  \nFund \nAllocatio\nn  \nExpenditur\ne  \nFund \nAllocatio\nn  \nExp\nAndhra \nPradesh   24007541   0   2425215\nArunachal \nP r a d e h    0  0  0  \nAssam   7900001   0   0   \nB i h a r    0  0  0  \nChandigarh   0   0   3678842   \nChhatisgarh   4428510   0       \nDelhi   3159844   0 9472436\nGoa  1985824 0   \nGujrat  8430374 0 300000\nHaryana   8772746   0   0   \nHimachal \nPradesh   1633334   0   0   \nJammu & \nKashmir   1243334   0   0   \nJharkhand   582353   0 2448484\nKarnataka   19033630   0   14171941   \nKerala   2140000   0   777000 