t": "Implementation of Agricultural Schemes", "head": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE,\n \nCOOPERATION\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n306\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \nTHE \n1\n9\nTH\n \n \nJULY\n, \n201\n6\n \n \nIMPLEMENTATION OF AGRICULTURAL\n \nSCHEMES\n \n \n306. \n \nSHRI\n \nANANDRAO ADSUL:\n \nSHRI DHARMENDRA\n \nYADAV:\n \nSHRI ADHALRAO PATIL\n \nSHIVAJIRAO:\n \nSHRI SHRIRANG APPA\n \nBARNE:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n  \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government is\n \nimplementing various schemes for thedevelopment of \nagriculture in the country\n \nand if so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether all the States do not show\n \nequal interest in agric\nulture and some States\n \nare slow \nin implementing the various\n \nagricultural schemes, if so, the details\n \nthereof;\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has issued\n \nany guidelines to those States which are\n \nslow in \nimplementing agricultural schemes;\n \n \n(d)\n \n \nif so, the detai\nls thereof along with\n \nthe response thereto; and\n \n \n(e)\n \n \nthe other steps taken by the\n \nGovernment to pursue the matter with\n \nthose States and \nspeed up the\n \nimplementation of these agricultural\n \nschemes?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAN\nD FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(SHRI\n  \nSUDARSHAN BHAGAT\n)\n    \n \n \n(a):\n \nAgriculture is a State Subject. However, the Government of India supports the State \nGovernments through various Central Sector and Centrally Sponsored\n \nSchemes for which \nfinancial assistance is provided in the sharing pattern of 60:40 between the Centre & the \nStates (90:10 in case of 8 North Eastern and 3 Himalayan States). A list of major schemes \nbeing implemented by the Department is at \nAnnexure \n–\n \nI\n.\n \n \n(b) \n \nto (e)\n:\n \n \nSome of the States are not able to fully utilize the allocated funds. A statement \nshowing the allocation of funds and expenditure incurred by various States during the \nfinancial year 2015\n-\n16 is at \nAnnexure \n–\n \nII\n. The Government of India regula\nrly monitors/ \nreviews progress of the Schemes through meetings with concerned officers of State \nGovernments to ensure efficient and judicious utilization of funds. Besides, zonal \nconferences, review meetings, video conferences are regularly held with the S\ntate Govt. \nand officers of the Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers’ Welfare visit the States to keep a close \nwatch on the implementation of various agricultural schemes.\n \n\n \n \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nS.No\n \n \nName of the Scheme\n \n \n \n1\n \nNational  Food Security Mission\n \n(NFSM)\n \n \n2\n \nNational Missi\non on Oilseeds & Oil Palm \n(NMOOP)\n \n \n3\n \nRainfed Area Development & Climate Change \n(RAD)\n \n4\n \nSoil Health Management\n \n(SHM)\n \n \n5\n \nSoil Health Card\n \n(SHC)\n \n \n6\n \nParamparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana\n \n(PKVY)\n \n \n7\n \nSub\n-\nmission on Agriculture Extension \n(SMAE)\n \n \n8\n \nNational E\n-\n \nGov\nerance Plan Agriculture\n \n \n \n9\n \nSub\n-\nmission on Agriculture Mechanization\n \n(SMAM)\n \n \n10\n \nSub\n-\n \nmission on Seeds and Planting Material\n \n(SMSP)\n \n \n11\n \nNational Horticulture Mission  \n(NHM)\n \n12\n \nNational Agroforesty & Bamboo Mission \n(NABM)\n \n \n13\n \nRashtriya Krishi Vikas Yoja\nna  \n(RKVY)\n \n \n14\n \nPradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana  \n(PMKSY)\n  \n[For Micro Irrigation]\n \n15\n \nHorticulture Mission for North East Himalayan States\n(HMN