.07.2016\t\n2455.25\n11. \t\nID‐P185\t\nState\t\nAgra\tWater\tSupply\t\nProject\t\n24822.00\t 30.03.2007\t\t/\t\n11.07.2017\t\n17707.83\nID‐P239\t Agra\tWater\tSupply\t\nProject\t(II)\t\n16279.00\t 31.03.2014\t/\t\n15.05.2020\t\n0.00\t\n12. \t ID‐P186\t State\t Amritsar\tSewerage\t\nProject\t\n6961.00\t 30.03.2007\t\t/\t\n11.07.2017\t\n3380.27\n13. \t ID‐P189\t State\t Goa\tWater\tSupply\t\nProject\t\n22806.00\t 14.09.2007\t/\t\n28.11.2017\t\n14492.34\t\n14. \t\nID‐P195\t\nState\t\nHogenakkal\tWater\t\nSupply\tand\tFuluorosis\t\nMitigation\tProject\t\n22387.00\t 10.03.2008\t/\t\n25.03.2017\t\n16605.45\t\nID"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |614", "t": "Gauge Conversion and Doubling of Railway Lines", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.614 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nGAUGE CONVERSION AND DOUBLING OF RAILWAY LINES \n \n†614.  SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV: \nSHRI KODIKUNNIL SURESH: \nSHRI BHAIRON PRASAD MISHRA: \nSHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT: \nSHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA: \n \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether there has been slow progress of gauge conversion and \ndoubling of railway lines; \n \n(b)  if so, whether any study has been conducted for ascertaining the \nreasons behind slow progress of these works; \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d)  the present status of gauge conversion and doubling of railway lines \nprojects including gauge conversion pro ject of Kollam -Chenkotta \nduring the last three years; \n \n(e)  whether any monthly targets have been set for all the 17 railway \nzones under corrective measures and if so, the details thereof along \nwith the achievements reflected as a result thereof; and \n \n(f)  the manner and the extent to which these measures are likely to \nspeed up the works in Railways? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (f):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n****** \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( f) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 614 BY SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV, SHRI KODIKUNNIL \nSURESH, SHRI BHAIRON PRASAD MISHRA, SHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT \nAND SHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 \nREGARDING GAUGE CONVERSION AND DOUBLING OF RAILWAY LINES \n \n(a) to (c):   The progress of commissioning of Gauge Conversion and \nDoubling Projects in last three years over Indian Railways is as given below:- \n \nYear Gauge Conversion (Km) Doubling (Km) \n2013-14 404 708 \n2014-15 527 705 \n2015-16 1042 972 \n \nFunds to the  ongoing Gauge Conversion and Doubling projects are \nallocated project-wise and zone -wise on year to year basis and allocation are \npresented alongwith cumulative expenditure in the form of Pink Book \nsubmitted to the Parliament along with the Budget Papers.  Project -wise \nbudget allotment is made as per availability of resources and progress of \nworks.  As the overall allocation was less in the past, all the projects could not \nbe allotted adequate funds, thereby affecting the progress adversely of  many \nprojects.  No special study has been carried out regarding progress of projects \nof Indian Railways. \n \n(d):   The status of gauge conversion and doubling projects  included in Works \nProgramme during the last three years i.e. 2013 -14, 2014-15 and 2015-16 is as \ngiven below:- \n \nPlah Head No. of Project (included in \nBudget in last three years) \nLength \n(in Km) \nLatest Cost \n(in Rs. Crores) \nGauge Conversion 2 176 821 \nDoubling 89 10,391 99,032 \n \n \n…2/- \n \n\n \n-2- \n \nThe present status of Kollam (Quilon)-Sengottai (Chenkotta) (95 Km) Gauge \nConversion project is as under:- \n \n(i)  Quilon -Punalur (45 Km) section is already commissioned.  Work has been \ntaken up on balance length Punalur-Kollam to Sengottai. \n \n(e) & (f):   Targets for Gauge Conversion and Doubling are fixed on yearly basis . \nOutlay for Gauge Conversion and Doubling Projects has been increased \nsubstantially in the last three years. However, to ensure steady progress \nthroughout the year and to address impediments, if any, faced by Zonal \nRailways, monthly monitoring is done for which such targets have also been \ncirculated.  \n \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |615", "t": "Bharat Net", "head": " \n  \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.615  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20 TH  JULY, 2016 \n \nBHARAT NET \n \n615.  SHRI RAJESH RANJAN: \nSHRI KALIKESH N. SINGH DEO: \nSHRIMATI POONAMBEN MAADAM: \nSHRI RAM MOHAN NAIDU KINJARAPU: \nSHRI A.T. NANA PATIL: \nSHRI C.R. PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the status of progress made under Bahrat Net P hase against the set target along with \nthe details of Gram Panchayats connected so far; \n \n(b)  whether the Government is considering the init iating of Phase II of the Bharat Net; \n \n(c)  whether any special feature is included for Ph ase II implementation in terms of \nstrengthening of Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV) as w ell as the monitoring mechanism and if \nso, the details thereof; \n \n(d)  whether the Government intends to engage any o ther agency/private sector in the \nprocess for efficient functioning and effective pro ject management and if so, the details \nthereof; and \n \n(e)  whether the Government has evaluated the perfo rmance of the three PSUs involved \nin the National Optical Fibre Network till date as compared to targets set, Statemwise and if so, \nthe details thereof, Statemwise and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) BharatNet project is planned to be implemented in phases. Under PhasemI of the \nproject, 1 lakh Gram Panchayats (GPs) are to be con nected by laying underground OFC by \nMarch 2017. The status of progress made under  BharatNet PhasemI , as on 09.07.2016, is \ngiven below:m \n \nItems  Planned  Achieved  \nPipe laid (km) 2,30,000 1,50,540 \nOFC pulled (km) 2,30,000 1,25,642 \nPipe laid (Gram Panchayats) 1,00,000 64,875 \nOptical Fibre Network (OFC) pulled (Gram \nPanchayats) \n1,00,000 54,023 \nConnectivity provided (Gram Panchayats) 1,00,000 7,312 \n  \n(b) to (d) Under PhasemII of BharatNet project, it is planned to provide connectivity to \nremaining 1.5 lakh GPs in the country using an opti mal mix of underground fibre, fibre over \npower lines, radio and satellite media, by December, 2018. The salient features of BharatNet \nPhasemII in terms of strengthening of Special Purpo se Vehicle (SPV) i.e. BBNL and \nmonitoring mechanism are at Annexure-I. \n \n(e) The performance of all the three CPSUs is being  monitored regularly at various levels. \nStatemwise performance of CPSUs in implementation of BharatNet is at Annexure-II.  \n \n \nContdcelipsis2/m \n \n \n\n \n  \n \n \n \nm2m \n \n \n \nAnnexure-I\n \n \nSalient features of  BharatNet  Phase-II in terms of strengthening of Special Purpose  \nVehicle (SPV) i.e. BBNL and monitoring mechanism  \n \n(i) Indian Institute of Technology (IIT), Bombay ha s been engaged as consultant to \nprovide media plan for radio and satellite broadban d connectivity to GPs for Phase II \nand other technology issues. \n(ii) Indian Institute of Management (IIM), Ahmedaba d is being engaged to provide \nroadmap for reorganization of BBNL for efficient fu nctioning and effective project \nmanagement. \n(iii) World Bank is being engaged to provide projec t management framework, recommend \nstandards and good practices for BharatNet management and rural broadband \ndemand assessment study and development of marketing strategies \n(iv) Fresh recruitment of manpower for field operat ions and management \n(v) Monitoring Mechanism of BBNL has been strengthe ned in April, 2016 with the setting \nup monitoring and issues resolution by three committees:  \n \n1. Empowered Committee to review progress and resol ution of policy level \nimplementation issues &  to meet once in a month. \n2. Steering Committee for resolution of intermagency implementation matters, to meet \nevery fortnight.  \n3. Technical Standing Committee for deciding the te chnology related issues \npertaining to BharatNet implementation. \n \n(vi) Mobile application based GIS monitoring system  is being developed for  capturing \nmonitoring data at field level with mobile devices to be displayed on GIS maps in \nrealtime.   \n \n \n \n \n \nCondtcelipsis.3/m \n \n  \n\n \n  \n \n \n \n \nm3m \n \nAnnexure-II \n \n \nStatewise status of BharatNet as on  09.07.2016 \n \n \nS.No.  States/ UTs  Executing \nCPSU \nNo. of Gram \nPanchayats \n(GPs)- Phase I \nPipe \nlaid \n(kms.) \nOptical \nFibre Cable \n(OFC) laid \n(in kms)  \nNo. of \nGPs \nwhere \nOFC laid  \nNo. of \nGPs lit \n1 Andaman & Nicobar BSNL 69 0 0 0 0 \n2 Andhra Pradesh PGCIL 0 1913 19 0 0 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh RailTel 256 594 100 22 0 \n4 Assam BSNL 1013 1986 1887 707 156 \n5 Bihar  BSNL  5202  7928  6915  2597  215  \n6 Chandigarh BSNL 12 18 19 12 12 \n7 Chhattisgarh BSNL 2110 5207 4982 1684 602 \n8 Goa*  m m m m m \n9 Gujarat RailTel 5735 7005 5395 2479 139 \n10  Haryana  BSNL  6090  5633  5481  3399  168  \n11 Himachal Pradesh PGCIL 283 232 128 44 0 \n12 Jammu & Kashmir BSNL 624 253 240 103 0 \n13 Jharkhand PGCIL 1388 2895 2685 1062 156 \n14 Karna"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |616", "t": "RPF Strength", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 616 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRPF STRENGTH \n \n†616.  SHRI SADASHIV LOKHANDE: \n        SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA:  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the present strength of personnel posted in the Railway \nProtection Force (RPF) is not adequate and a large number of \nrailway stations do not have women police personnel; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof ; \n \n(c) whether the Government had previously planned to place \nadequate number of women police in all railway station s across \nthe country;  \n \n(d) if so, the present status of the said proposal and the number of \npersonnel including women police posted in railway stations \nacross the country during the last three years; and \n \n(e) the details of the broad guidelines issued to RPF for the safety and \nsecurity of railway passengers and their luggage? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a) to ( d) : The present sanctioned strength of 75,879 of RPF staff is \nadequate as per present requirement, since the security in the \n\nRailways is looked after by Railway Protection Force (RPF), Govt. \nRailway Police (GRP) and local police.  \n With a view to increase the strength of women personnel in RPF, a \nprovision has been made to reserve 10% of the vacancies for women in \nall initial recruitments. 1014 women personnel have been recruited in \nlast 03 years and total strength of women personnel  has now been \nincreased from 1327 to 2341 at present.  \n  On an average approx 38798 Males and 1834 Females are deployed \non the Railway Stations across the country. \n  \n(e) Instructions for safety and security of Railway passengers and their \nluggage have been issued by Railway Board. In addition steps have also \nbeen taken by the Railways for the safety and security of Railway \npassengers. The guidelines cover the followings:-  \n1. Deployment of escort party of RPF in important trains for safety \nand security of passengers and their luggage. \n2. Deployment of special squad consisting of RPF personnel including \nwomen for women security.  \n3.  Help Line number 182 has been operationalised for providing \nsecurity related assistance round the clock to passengers. \n4. To coordinate wit h the GRP/Police authorities at all levels to \nensure proper registration and investigation of the case of crime. \n5. To launch regular drives under the provisions of the Railways Act, \n1989 to preven t unauthorized entry in trains and  in railway \npremises.  \n 6. Surveillance by CCTV at selected Railway stations to prevent    \ncrime.   \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |617", "t": "Inhuman Behaviour with Indians Abroad", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.617    \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINHUMAN BEHAVIOUR WITH INDIANS ABROAD \n \n617.   SHRI RAHUL SHEWALE:  \nSHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS:  \nSHRI SANJAY DHOTRE:  \nSHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether there has been an increase/ decrease in the cases of \nexploitation/torture of Indian workers working in other \ncountries; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the number of such cases \nreported upon across the world during each of the last three \nyears and the current year, country-wise; \n \n(c) whether the Government has also received complaints about \nphysical and sexual abuse of domestic workers working in \nother countries during the said period;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof, country-wise; \n \n(e) whether the Government has taken up the issue with the \nforeign countries concerned; and  \n \n(f) if so, the details and the outcome thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) Information regarding Indian workers holding ECR \nPassports, going for overseas employment to 18 notified Emigration \nCheck Required (ECR) countries (Afghanistan, Bahrain, Indonesia, \nIraq, Jordan, Kuwait, Lebanon, Libya, Mal aysia, Oman, Qatar, North \nSudan, South Sudan, Syria, Thailand, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, \n\nUnited Arab Emirates and Yemen), is maintained by this Ministry. As \nper information available with the Indian Missions/Posts in ECR \ncountries, there is no general pattern to indicate an increase in \ncases of exploitation/ torture of Indian workers. Details of \ncomplaints received during the last three years and current year are \nat Annexure. \n \n(c) & (d)   Most of the complaints received from Indian workers,  \nincluding  domestic workers, from time to time, are generally in the \nnature of non -payment/ delayed payment or underpayment of \nsalaries, long working hours, inadequate living conditions, physical \nharassment, non-renewal of visa and labour card on time, refusal to \npay for the medical treatment, denial of leave and air -ticket to the \nhometown on completion of contract period, forcible custody of \nPassport and Visa, refusal of leave or ‘exit/re -entry permits’/‘final \nexit visa’ etc. No specific complaint of sexual abuse has  been \nreported by the Missions.   \n \nSuch complaints are addressed by the Indian Missions by \ntaking them up with the concerned foreign authorities , Foreign \nEmployers or the officials of the Labour Ministry of that country.   \n \n(e) & (f)   Whenever the Indian Missions are approached by any \nIndian national in distress, the same is followed up, at various \nlevels, with the authorities concerned in the Governments of the \nrespective country.  In addition, Government of India has signed \nMoUs with 6 Gulf countries, na mely UAE, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman, \nBahrain, Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and Malaysia. As per these MoUs, \nthe host country will take measures for protection and welfare of \nthe workers in organized sector. The recruitment and terms of \nemployment will be in conformit y with the laws of both the \ncountries. \n  \nThese MOUs are renewed / signed afresh, from time to time, \nduring which process any modifications are duly considered for \ninclusion. \n \n The Government of India has set up Indian Community Welfare \nFund (ICWF) in all t he Indian Missions/consulates abroad to meet \ncontingency expenditure incurred by them for carrying out various \nwelfare activities for overseas Indian citizens who are in distress. \nThe objectives of the ICWF include:- \n  \n\n(i) Boarding and lodging for distressed O verseas Indians in \nneed; \n \n(ii) Extending emergency medical care to the Overseas Indians \nin need; \n \n(iii) Providing air passage to stranded Overseas Indians in need; \n \n(iv) Providing initial legal assistance to the Overseas Indians in \ndeserving cases; \n \n(v) Expenditure on incidentals and for airlifting the mortal \nremains to India or local cremation/burial of the deceased \nOverseas Indians in such cases where the sponsor is unable \nor unwilling to do so as per the contract and the family is \nunable to meet the cost; \n \n(vi) Providing the payment of penalties in respect of Indian \nnationals for illegal stay in the host country where prima \nfacie the worker is not at fault; \n \n(vii) Providing the payment of small fines/penalties for the release \nof Indian nationals in jail/detention centre; \n \n The Ministry has set up a 24X7 Helpline ‘Overseas Workers \nResource Centre (OWRC)’ based in Gurgaon, Haryana which provides \ninformation and guidance on all matters and problems pertaining to \noverseas employment of Indian nationals.  Indian Workers Resource \nCentre (IWRC) set up in Dubai by Embassy of India, in UAE, provides \nguidance and counseling on all matters pertaining to overseas \nIndian workers in UAE. Shelter homes for distressed Indian \nnationals, have been set up in"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |618", "t": "Attack on Indians", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.618 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nATTACK ON INDIANS \n \n618.     KUMARI SUSHMITA DEV:  \nSHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA: \n \n Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that the recent spate of attacks \nagainst the African community in India and reprisal attacks against \nIndians in Africa has invited Global attention; \n \n(b)    if so, the details thereof and whether the Union Govern ment has \nfailed in preventing such attacks on Africans;  \n \n(c) If so, the reasons therefor; and  \n \n(d) the steps taken by the Government to ensure safety of students \nfrom Africa in various parts of the country? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M.J. AKBAR) \n \n(a) to (c) The recent incidents relating to the members of African \ncommunity in India were not premeditated acts against a particular \ncommunity. These were spontaneous attacks perpetrated by anti -social \nand criminal e lements.  Two of the three perpetrators of the killing of \nCongolese national were swiftly apprehended. Government of Democratic \nRepublic of Congo also acted swiftly to control reprisal attacks against \nIndians in Kinshasa. India’s historical relations with Africa rest on the \nfoundation of brotherhood and solidarity  and such incidents cannot be \nallowed to deflect from India’s historical friendship and close \ndevelopment partnership with Africa.  \n \n(d)  Ministry of External Affairs proactively reached out to the  African \ndiplomatic and student community. It was requested that police \npatrolling be increased in areas where sizeable African community  \nresides. It has also been decided to hold regular meetings with the \nAfrican community in all major metropolitan cities . The State \ngovernments, having large numbers of African nationals,  have also been \nrequested to take steps to ensure their safety and security. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |619", "t": "Welfare Schemes for Minorities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.619 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nWelfare Schemes for Minorities \n \n \n 619.  SHRI DHARAMBIR: \nSHRI GEORGE BAKER: \nDR. MANOJ RAJORIA: \nSHRI P.K. BIJU: \n \n \n Will the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of various schemes under implementation for the welfare of minorities; \n \n(b) the funds allocated/released/spent for implementation of these schemes during each of the last \nthree years and the current year, scheme-wise, State/UT-wise; \n \n(c)  the targets fixed/achieved and the number of persons benefitted under these schemes during \nthe above period, State/UT-wise, scheme-wise; and \n \n(d) the steps taken by the Government for speedy implementation and to achieve the targets  under \nthe said schemes and to create awareness about such schemes? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF \nMINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a) to (c) This Ministry implements the following schemes for the welfare of minorities:  \n(i) The Multi-sectoral Development Programme (MsDP)  aims at improving the socio -\neconomic condition and providing basic amenities for improving the quality of life of minorities. \nThe State/UT wise details of fund released during the last three years and current year is at \nAnnexure -I. \n  \nNo physical targets are fixed by this  Ministry under MsDP. Projects are approved on the basis of \nthe project proposals received from the States/UTs as per their requirement s. Under MsDP, assets \nare created for the welfare of the community as a whole and not for individuals. \n \n(ii) Pre-matric Scholarship Scheme - The scholarship is provided to  minority students \nstudying in C lass I to X in recognized Government/Private schools. Minimum 30% \nscholarships are earmarked for girls.  \n\n(iii) Post-matric Scholarship Scheme - The scholarship is provided to  minority students \nstudying in C lass XI to Ph.D level in recognized Government/Private \nschools/Colleges/Institutes. Minimum 30% scholarships are earmarked for girls.  \n The State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Pre-matric \nScholarship Scheme and Post -matric Scholarship Scheme may please be seen at Annexure \n–II.  \n(iv) Merit-cum-Means based Scholarship Scheme - The merit -cum-means scholarship \nscheme is awarded for pursuing professional and technical courses, at under -graduate and \npost-graduate levels, in institutions recognized by the appropriate authority. Under the \nscheme, 30% of these scholarships are earmarked for girl students. 85 institutes for \nprofessional and technical courses have been listed in the scheme.  \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Scheme \nmay please be seen at Annexure – III.  \n \n(v)    Maulana Azad National Fellowship - The objective of th e Fellowship is to provide \nintegrated five year fellowships in the form of financial assistance to students from \nminority communities to pursue higher studies such as M.Phil and Ph.D. It is implemented \nthrough University Grant s Commission (UGC). Fellowship s are awarded  to research \nstudents pursuing regular and full time M.Phil and Ph.D. courses.  \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Scheme \nmay please be seen at Annexure – IV.  \n \n(vi)  Free Coaching & Allied Scheme - The objectives of the scheme are to assist students \nbelonging to the minority communities by way of special coaching for (a) qualifying \nexaminations for admission in technical/ professional courses such as engineering, law, \nmedical, management, informatio n technology etc. (b) Competitive examinations for \nrecruitment to Group „A‟ , „B‟ and „C‟ services and other equivalent posts under the \nCentral and State governments including public sector undertakings, banks, insurance \ncompanies as well as autonomous bodies.  \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Scheme \nmay please be seen at Annexure – V.  \n \n(vii) Support to minority candidates clearing Prelims conducted by UPSC/SSC, State \nPublic Service Commission (PSC) etc. - The objective of the Scheme is to provide \nfinancial support to the minority candidates clearing prelims conducted by Union Public \nService Commission, Staff Selection Commission and State Public Service Commissions \nto adequately equip them to compete for appoi ntment to Civil Services in the Union and \nthe State Governments and to increase th e representation of the minorities  in the Civil \nServices by giving direct financial support to candidates clearing Preliminary Examination  \nof Group A and B (Gazetted and no n-Gazetted posts of Union Public Service Commission \n(UPSC); State Public Service Commissions (SPSCs) and Staff Selection Commission \n(SSC) etc.  \n\n(viii) Padho Pardesh - Interest Subsidy on Educational Loans for overseas studies - The \nobjective of the scheme i s to a"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |62", "t": "Unorganised Workers in EPFO", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES, \nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*62 \nANSWERED ON 21.07.2016 \n \nFLOOD MANAGEMENT PROJECTS  \n*62.   SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR SINGH \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA \nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:  \n(a) the details of flood management projects completed during the current Five Year Plan period and \nthe benefit accrued as a result thereof; \n(b) the detail s of the ongoing, pending and proposed flood mitigation projects in the country, \nState/UT-wise;  \n(c) the financial and physical targets and the achievements thereof under such projects, State/UT-wise;  \n(d) whether any specific measures have been taken by t he Government to check excessive rain water \nand flood in the country, especially in the current monsoon season particularly for Bihar; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof, State/ UT-wise? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA  \nREJUVENATION \n(SUSHRI UMA BHARTI) \n \n(a) to (e) :  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF STARRED QUESTION \nNo. 62 (Priority No. 2) FOR ANSWER ON 21.07.2016 REGARDING “FLOOD \nMANAGEMENT PROJECTS” \n(a) to (c) Under the Flood Management Programme (FMP) in a total of 519 projects have been \napproved during the XI and XII Plan, out of which 297 projects have been completed till date. The \ncompleted projects have provided reasonable protection agains t floods in 19.59 lakh hectare area and \nbenefited 197.23 lakh people in the country.   \n \nThe State- wise details of projects approved, projects completed and area protected under Flood \nManagement Programme (FMP) so far are given at Annex-1 & 2 respectively.  \n \nThe Ministry also provide s technical guidance to State Governments through the expert agencies --\nCentral Water Commission (CWC) and Ganga Flood Control Commission ( GFCC) in formulation of \nflood management projects. During the XII Plan, a total of 537 projects were received for techno -\neconomic appraisal out of which 256 projects were cleared by  the appraisal agencies. The State- wise \ndetails are given at Annex-3.  \n \nOut of the  techno-economically cleared 256 projects, 99 projects for Rs. 5344.15crore have been \napproved under Flood Management Programme (FMP ). A total central assistance of Rs.4723.08 crore \nhas been released to various States till date, which includes Rs. 907.82 crores for Bihar. \n \n(d) & (e) The subject of f lood management being under the purview of the States, the schemes for \nflood control are formulated and implemented by concerned States as per their priority. The Union \nGovernment supplements the efforts of the States by providing technical guidance and also \npromotional financial assistance for management of floods in critical areas. In addition, during XII \nPlan, the Ministry has approved a plan scheme for Rs.281 crore for flood forecasting, modernisation \nand expansion of the flood forecasting network for automat ic data collection, expeditious transmission \nand flood forecast dissemination. The scheme has the following components; \n \ni) The Flood Forecasting network is proposed to be expanded from existing 183 flood forecasting \nstations to 275 stations  as per details in  Annexure 4. Simultaneously, the support network of \n708 hydrological observation sites would be increased to 1118.  The entire network of 1118 \nstations would be on an automatic satellite based telemetry system.  Currently only 507 stations \nare having telemetry facility. As a result of the telemetry network, live information would be \navailable on the real time basis.  It will eliminate the delays in dissemination of flood warnings \nto the States due to the manual system of dissemination. \n\n \nii) All the 12 regio nal offices of CWC will have the facility of carrying out data modeling for \nmaking timely forecasts to forewarn the community and the local authorities with lead time \nupto 72 hours before occurrence of the event.  This is in contrast with the existing fore cast lead \ntime of 24 hours. \n \niii) The enhanced network will ensure coverage of the hitherto uncovered additional regions in \nsub-basins of Ganga, Brahmaputra, Mahanadi& Godavari, which are amongst highly flood \nprone areas and experience huge flood damages. \n \niv) It is also proposed to provide inundation forecast on pilot basis in 3 mha flood prone area of \nKosi, Brahmaputra, Godavari and Sabri sub- basins using high resolution Digital Elevation \nModels already available with National Remote Sensing Centre. \n \nv) Currently, on an average 6000 flood warnings are issued annually with an accuracy of over \n98%.  It is expected that with expanded network of flood forecast systems, these would go upto \n10,000 annual warnings covering hitherto uncovered areas in the basins mentioned above, with \nan enhanced lead time of upto 72 hours. This would give community enough time to"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |620", "t": "Railway University", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 620 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRAILWAY UNIVERSITY \n \n620.    SHRI RAOSAHEB DANVE PATIL : \n  SHRI GEORGE BAKER : \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the present status of the  railway university proposed to be set \nup in the country; \n \n(b) the details of the funds earmarked for the purpose; \n \n(c) the details of the expenditure likely to be incurred thereon along \nwith the resources from where it is proposed to be raised; \n \n(d) whether some foreign countries have offered assistance for this \npurpose; \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by the Railways in \nthis regard; and \n \n(f) the time-frame fixed, if any, for setting up the university? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) Ministry of Railways have decided to establish one Railway \nUniversity by   upgrading   National   Academy  of   Indian  Railways  at  \nContd…2/- \n\n-2- \n \nVadodara and by incorporating the existing Centralised Training \nInstitutes of Indian Railways as Constituent Schools of Study. \n \n(b) A token outlay of ₹ 10 lakhs has been provided in the Railway \nBudget 2016-17 for this purpose. \n \n(c) A capital cost of ₹ 861 crores is envisaged for the University. \nHowever, details of expenditure likely to be incurred and resources for \nthe proposed University have not been worked out at this stage. \n \n(d) No, Madam.  \n \n(e) Does not arise. \n \n(f) No time frame has been fixed. \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |621", "t": "Rail Victim Compensation Fund", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 621 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n        RAIL VICTIM COMPENSATION FUND \n \n621.     SHRI GUTHA SUKENDER REDDY: \n   SHRI SANGANNA AMARAPPA: \n    SHRI ABHISHEK SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether the Government has received any proposal of creating \nRail Victim Compensation Fund to provide compensation to the \npersons suffered under rail accidents; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the further action taken by the Government in this regard; \n \n(d)  the details of guidelines regarding payment of compensation to \nthe rail accident victims; and \n \n(e)    the details of accidents that took place during the last two years \nand the current year due to poor maintenance of ra ilway lines and the \naction taken by the Railways in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n ( SHRI MANOJ SINHA ) \n \n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n**** \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 621 BY SHRI GUTHA SUKENDER REDDY, \nSHRI SANGANNA AMARAPPA AND SHRI ABHISHEK SINGH TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07. 2016 REGARDING RAIL VICTIM \nCOMPENSATION FUND \n \n(a) to (c) : Yes Madam. A representation has recently been received \nfrom an Hon’ble Member of Parliament proposing creation of Rail \nVictim Compensation Fund to provide adequate compensation to \nvictims of rail a ccidents by levy of an additional charge on passenger \nfare. The proposal contained in the representation is under \nexamination in this Ministry. \n \n(d) : In terms of Section 125 of the Railways Act, 1989, and Section 16 \nof the Railway Claims Tribunal Act, 198 7, the claimant of the \ncompensation for death/injury in Train Accident / Untoward Incident \nhas to move an application for compensation in the Railway Claims \nTribunal.  The compensation is paid by the Railways after a decree is \nawarded by the Tribunal in fa vour of the claimant subject to \nsatisfaction of Railway. \n      Time limit for filing claims for train accident is one year from the \ndate of occurrence which can be condoned by the Railway Claim \nTribunal, if sufficient reason is shown. \n \n                ...2/- \n\n \n-2- \n(e) : Number of consequential train accidents on Engineering account \nthat took place during the last two years and the current year upto \n15.07.2016 is given below:- \nYear Responsibility Total \n2014-15 \nOn Engineering Account 27 \nEngineering dept. jointly with other Dept. 9 \nGrand Total 36 \n2015-16 \nOn Engineering Account 26 \nEngineering dept. jointly with other Dept. 12 \nGrand Total 38 \n2016-17 \n(Up to 15th \nJuly, 2016) \nOn Engineering Account 8 \nEngineering dept. jointly with other Dept. 1 \nGrand Total 9 \n \n       Measures are being undertaken on continuing basis for upkeep of \ntracks to prevent accidents which includes replacement of over -aged \nassets, adoption to suitable technologies for up -gradation and \nmaintenance of track. Safety drives and inspections at  regular \nintervals are carried out to monitor and educate staff for observance \nof safe practices. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |622", "t": "Rail Connectivity with Neighbouring Countries", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 622 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n \nRAIL CONNECTIVITY WITH NEIGHBOURING COUNTRIES \n \n \n622. SHRI S. SELVAKUMARA CHINNAYAN: \n SHRI P. NAGARAJAN: \n   \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether the Railways has any proposal to connect India by rail with \nChina through Tibet and Nepal in the near future; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)   the time by which the said proposal is likely to be implemented? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \n \n \n \n    (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n \n(a):  No, Madam.   \n \n(b) & (c):  Do not arise. \n \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |623", "t": "Railway Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.623 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n623.  DR. KULAMANI SAMAL: \nSHRI KIRTI AZAD: \nSHRI M. RAJA MOHAN REDDY: \nSHRI RAJU SHETTY: \nSHRIMATI NEELAM SONKER: \nSHRI P.K. BIJU: \nSHRI ALOK SANJAR: \nSHRI RAVINDRA KUMAR PANDEY: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n (a)  the details of the railway projects sanctioned during the last two years and \nthe current year, Zone/State-wise, project-wise and year-wise; \n  \n(b)  the present status of various new/ongoing/pending railway projects and \nsurveys in the country during the above period, Zone/State-wise and project-\nwise; \n  \n(c)  the funds allocated and expenditure incurred on each of the projects during \nthe said period, Zone/State-wise, project -wise and year-wise;  \n \n(d)  whether the Railways proposes to give more financial assistance to the rail \nprojects in the States particularly in Kerala and if so, the details thereof;   \n(e)  whether the Railways has received complaints reg arding substandard and \nlow grade materials being used in some rail projects in the country including \nOdisha and if so, the details thereof and the action taken thereon;  \n(f)  whether the Railways has constituted any committee to monitor the \nimplementation of these projects and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(g)  the steps taken/being taken by the Railways for expeditious completion of \nsuch projects?  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n  \n(a) to (g):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( g) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 623 BY DR. KULAMANI SAMAL, SHRI KIRTI AZAD, SHRI M. \nRAJA MOHAN REDDY, SHRI RAJU SHETTY, SHRIMATI NEELAM SONKER, SHRI \nP.K. BIJU, SHRI ALOK SANJAR AND SHRI RAVINDRA KUMAR PANDEY TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n(a) to (c):   Details of all those railway projects sanctioned during the last two \nyears and the current year i.e. 2014 -15, 2015 -16 & 2016 -17 including Cost, \nLength, Fund allotment, Expenditure etc. are available in public domain on \nIndian Railways website i.e. www.indianr ailways.gov.in and are also available \nin Pink Book s presented before the House alongwith Budget papers  for all \nthese years.   \n \n(d):   Funds to the various railway projects are allocated project -wise and \nzone-wise on year to year basis and allocation s are presented alongwith \ncumulative expenditure in the form of Pink Book submitted to the House along \nwith the Budget Papers.  Project -wise budget allotment is made as per \navailability of resources  and progress of work .  In particular , allocation of    \n`45 Crore for new line, `181 Crore for Gauge Conversion and `790 Crore for \nDoubling projects falling fully/partly in State of Kerala have been made in Rail \nBudget 2016-17.   \n \n(e):   System is in place to ensure quality control in execution of projects.  \nTherefore, adherence to q uality in railway projects is a continuous process.  \nComplaints regarding use of substandard material in railway projects, \nwhenever received, are investigated / inquired into and corrective action  and \nsystem improvement, if any, are taken as required.   \n \n(f):   No separate committee has been framed to monitor the implementation \nof railway projects.  The monitoring is done  at different levels from field units \nto Railway Board and above at regular intervals.   \n…2/- \n\n \n-2- \n \n(g):   Some other steps taken/being taken by the Government for effective and \nspeedy implementation of rail projects in the country are (i) substantial \nincrease in allocation of funds, (ii) prioritization of projects, (iii) delegation  of \npowers at field level, (iv) regular co-ordination meetings with State \nGovernments for land acquisition, relocation of utilities, etc. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |624", "t": "Clearances to Railway Projects", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.624 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n \nCLEARANCES TO RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n \n624.  SHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB: \nSHRI SANJAY DHOTRE: \nSHRI RAHUL SHEWALE: \n \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a)  the number of railway projects stalled due to lack of clearances \nfrom the department of environment/forest along with the amount \nstuck therein across the country, as on date, Zone/State/Union \nterritory-wise; \n  \n(b)  whether the Railways have suffered losses on  account of being \ndormant in earning revenue from such projects and their cost \nescalation over a period of time; \n  \n(c)  if so, the details thereof, project-wise and the reasons therefor along \nwith the reaction of the Railways thereto; \n  \n(d)  whether the Ra ilways did not obtain prior clearances from the \ndepartment of environment/forest for these projects; and \n  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?  \n  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (e):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF UNSTARRED QUESTION \nNO. 624 BY SHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB, SHRI SANJAY DHOTRE AND SHRI RAHUL \nSHEWALE TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING \nCLEARANCES TO RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n(a) to (c): Clearances from different land owning agencies, acquisition of land, shifting \nof services/utilities are part of project execution and these activities are bound to \ntake some time.  However, following projects have suffered due to non availability of \nforest clearances.   \nS. \nNo. \nState Railway Name of the Project \n1 Bihar  Eastern Doubling between Ratanpur-Jamalpur \n(Part of Munger Bridge approach track) \n2 Jharkhand East Central Tori- Shivpur-Kathautia New Line \n3 Bihar  East Central Sakri -Biraul-Kusheshwarsthan-\nHasanpur Road New Line \n4 Odisha  East Coast Angul-Sukhinda Road New Line \n5 Odisha  East Coast Byepass line bet. Sukhinda Road and \nJajpur Keonjhar Road \n6 Sikkim, West \nBengal \nNortheast Frontier Sivok-Rangpo New Line \n7 Assam Northeast Frontier New Moynaguri-Jogighopa New Line \n8 Kerala Southern Angamali - Sabarimala New Line \n9 Maharashtra South Central Ratlam-Khandwa-Akola Gauge \nConversion \n10 Chhattisgarh South East Central Gondia-Jabalpur Gauge Conversion \n11 Chhatisgarh South East Central Dallirajahara-Rowghat New Line \n12 Chhatisgarh South East Central Salka Road- Annupur Doubling \n13 Karnataka  South Western Hubli-Ankola New Line \n14 Karnataka  South Western Bangalore- Satyamangalam  New Line \n15 Madhya Pradesh \n& Uttar Pradesh \nWest Central Lalitpur-Singrauli New Line \n \nWorking out cost escalation o r revenue loss on account of delay in forest \nclearance alone is not feasible to be worked out.  \n \n(d) & (e):   Railway being one of the most environment friendly means of transport \ndoes not require environment clearance for undertaking projects .  Proposal fo r \ndiversion of forest land and tree cutting, wherever needed , can only be prepared \nonly after detailed survey, pegging of alignment and preparation of land schedule.   \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |625", "t": "Indian Sailors Killed in Oman", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.625 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINDIAN SAILORS KILLED IN OMAN \n \n625.   SHRI P. NAGARAJAN: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether 2 Indian sailors were killed  and 3 people including pilot \nwere injured during the recent oil tanker fire at the port of Oman; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)   whether the Indian Embassy in Oman has provided necessary \nassistance to those Indians killed and injured in the accident;  \n \n(d)   if so, the details thereof; \n \n(e)  whether the Government has taken up this issue with the Oman \nauthority and the shipping company to provide due compensation to \nthose Indians who died in the fire; and  \n \n(f)    if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) Yes. Two Indian crew members died and three other crew \nmembers suffered burn injuries when an oil tanker caught fire in the \nengine room while at a dock on the border between Oman and Yemen. \n  \n(c) & (d) The Embassy of India in Oman facilitated the transportation \nand airlifting of mortal remains of the two crew members  to India and the \ntreatment of the injured crew members was carried out in Royal Hospital, \nSalalah by the managing company M/s Etihad Engin eering & Marine \nServices, UAE. \n  \n(e) & (f) M/s Etihad Engineering & Marine Services, UAE  has informed \nthe Embassy of India  in Oman that the compensation for the crew \nmembers, who died in the accident in the Engine room of the oil tanker , \nhas been paid by them to their families. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |626", "t": "Director Level Officers", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF PERSONNEL & TRAINING) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 626 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016) \n \nDIRECTOR LEVEL OFFICERS \n \n†626. SHRI VISHNU DAYAL RAM: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the actual number of officers serving as Directors in Indian Administrative Service \nwho belong to Scheduled Castes (SC)/Scheduled Tribes (ST); \n \n(b)  whether the officers belonging to SC/ST have not been included in the Joint Secretary \npanel with their colleagues from the same batch; \n \n(c)  if so, the number of such officers along with the reasons therefor; and \n \n(d)  the number of officers belonging to SC/ST wh o have been included in the panel for \nthe post of Joint Secretary during the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions and Minister \nof State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a):   Presently, there are 38 IAS officers working at Director level in Government of India \nunder the Central Staffing Scheme; of which 6 officers belong to SC category and 1 officer \nbelongs to ST Category. \n \n(b) to (d):   The Panels for appointment at J oint Secretary level are prepared on the basis of \nexperience, suitability for appropriate consideration of Civil Services Board out of the \nofficers empanelled to hold Joint Secretary level posts including SC & ST officers. Further, \nin the last three years,  total 29 IAS officers from SC category and 15 IAS officers from ST \ncategory have been empanelled for holding Joint Secretary level posts at the Centre. Further, \nat present, 20 SC and 7 ST IAS officers are working at Joint Secretary level in various \nMinistries/Departments of Government of India under the Central Staffing Scheme. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |627", "t": "Under Water Robot", "head": " \n                                             \n                                           GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 627 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 20, 2016 \n \nUNDER WATER ROBOT \n \n627. DR. MANOJ RAJORIA: \n \n        Will the Minister of EARTH SCIENCES be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has formulated a scheme/project to deploy under \nwater robots in the Bay of Bengal; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and its likely benefits to the general public and farmers; \n(c)   whether foreign assistance is being sought for the said project; and \n(d)    if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND  \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y. S. CHOWDARY) \n \n(a) No Madam. However, an Ocean Glider has been deployed. \n(b) In order to improve the oceanographic observation data in the Bay of Bengal  as \napart of ongoing Ocean Observing System Program , a Glider has been acquired \nby the Indian National Center for Ocean Information services (INCOIS), \nHyderabad. Ocean Glider, an au tonomous, unmanned underwater vehicle  is, \nused to measure various oceanographic parameters such as temperature, \nsalinity, chlorophyll and photosynthetically active radiation along a desired \ntrack in the upper 1000 m of water column. At the end of each dive -and-climb \nphase Glider transmit collected data to the base -station at land via satellite \ntelemetry. Repeated hydrographic survey in the international waters of the \nnorthern Bay of Bengal (18°N, 89.5°E) were conducted during the period of 3 rd \nSeptember, 2015 to 10 th January, 2016 using this Glider and the vehicle has \nbeen successfully recovered after the mission.  Gliders are also used recently \nduring the joint research campaign between India and United Kingdom (U.K.) \nover the Bay of Bengal to understand monsoon ocean process. \n \nOverall improvement to the monsoon forecast will help the economic growth \nparticularly though improved incomes to the larger community depending on \nagricultural activities.  \n(c-d) As the Glider technology  is new , three s cientists from INCOIS have been \ndeputed for two week Glider training at Kongsberg Underwater Technology inc., \nLynnwood, Seattle, USA and Applied Physics Laboratory (APL), University of \nWashington, Seattle, USA. Moreover, during the initial phase of Glider mission, \nINCOIS scientist operated the vehicle under the supervision of APL scientists \nand the team is successfully completed the glider mission outside Indian \nexclusive economic zone (EEZ).  \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |628", "t": "Electrification of Railway Line", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 628 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nELECTRIFICATION OF RAILWAY LINE  \n \n628.  SHRIMATI P.K. SREEMATHI TEACHER:        \n            \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether there is inordinate delay in completion of electrification  \nof Kozhikode-Mangalore railway line; \n \n(b)    if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and \n \n(c)   the  steps taken by the Railways for the speedy completion of  \nabove work and the time by which the said project is likely to be \ncompleted? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a): No, Madam. \n \n(b): Does not arise. \n \n(c):Shoranur-Kozhikode-Charvattur section has already been \ncommissioned on electric traction and electrification of Charvattur -\nMangalore section is planned for commissioning by Decemb er 2016. \nFurther t o expedite electrification  of Kozhikode -Mangalore railway \nline, improved project monitoring mechanism has been introduced and \nadequate funding through Extra Budgetary Resources (Institutional \nFinance) has been provided.   \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |629", "t": "Science and Technology Demonstration Centres", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nDEPARTMENT OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.629 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20/07/2016 \n \nSCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY DEMONSTRATION CENTRES \n \n629. SHRI C. MAHENDRAN: \n \nWill the Minister of SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY òãðìððÐð ¡ðøÜ ÑßðøÌðð÷ò±ð¨îó Ùðüëðó \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to develop Science and Technology demonstration \ncentres in all districts to impart scientific temper among students and people;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the locations identified for the purpose; \n \n(c) the benefits likely to accrue therefrom; \n \n(d) whether any special Science and Technology projects/schemes are proposed in various \nStates including the State of Tamil Nadu; and  \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y.S. CHOWDARY) \nòãðìððÐð ¡ðøÜ ÑßðøÌðð÷ò±ð¨îó ÙðüëððâðÚð Ùð÷ü Üð¸Úð Ùðüëðó +ÉÉè® ÑðöÆãðó òãðìððÐð ÙðüëððâðÚð Ùð÷ü Üð¸Úð Ùðüëðó \n (gÉÉÒ ´ÉÉ<Ç. AºÉ. SÉÉèvÉ®ÉÒ) \n \n \n(a) No, Madam. \n \n(b) & (c):   Do not arise. \n  \n(d) No, Madam.  \n \n(e) Does not arise. \n \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |63", "t": "State Education System", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.63 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2016 \nState Education System \n \n63. SHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has noticed that the recent exam scam in the State of \nBihar has exposed the underbelly of the education system in the States \nthroughout the country;  \n \n(b) if so, whether in view of scams in various States education system, the \nGovernment proposes to taken monitoring or other steps to check such exam \nscams particularly at Senior and Higher Secondary School levels in the country; \nand  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a) : The incident of a scam in Bihar School Education Board has come to the \nnotice of the Government. However, isolated incidents cannot be taken as \nyardstick for the education system in the States throughout the country. Also, \nState Education Boards come under the administrative control of respective State \nGovernments.   This Ministry organizes consultation with Central and State \nExamination Boards from time to time to evolve sound practices. The National \nCurriculum Framework (NCF-2005) emphasizes the need to shift from content \nbased testing to problem solving and competency based testing.  \n(b) & (c): There is no proposal at present with this Ministry to monitor the \nactivities of State Education Boards.  It is for the State Government concerned to \ndo so. This Ministry facilitates interaction among Boards on important issues.  \nFurther, the National Curriculum Framework has enunciated general principles \non Examination Reforms. \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |630", "t": "Attack on African Nationals in India", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.630 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nATTACK ON AFRICAN NATIONALS IN INDIA \n \n630.     SHRI HUKUM SINGH: \n \n Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether African diplomats have boycotted some events scheduled by the \nIndian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR) recently in Delhi and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(b)    whether the Government did an outreach event with African students \nalong with concerned embassies to reassure them of safety and would \nmeet the African Heads of Mission every three months and if so, the \ndetails thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the African Group of Heads of Mission also decided to \nrecommend to their Government not to send new students to India due to \nstereotyping and racial prejudice due to the recent murder of the \nCongolese students in India and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(d) the present status of the safety and security of African nationals in India? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M.J. AKBAR) \n \n(a)  No. African diplomats did not boycott some events scheduled by the \nIndian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR) recently in Delhi. African diplomats \nparticipated in the “Africa Day” celebrations organized by ICCR on 26 May \n2016.  \n \n(b)    Yes, Hon’ble  External Affairs Minister, Minister of State for External \nAffairs and senior officials met African diplomatic and student community to \nassure them of their safety and security . Minister of State of External Affairs \nwould be having a quarterly meeting with the African Heads of Mission.  \n \n(c) No. I t has not come to our notice. African Heads of Mission have \nexpressed their appreciation for the prompt action taken by G overnment of \nIndia related to recent spontaneous and isolated incidents against members of \nthe African community. \n \n(d) The State governments, having large numbers of African nationals, have \nbeen requested to take steps to ensure their safety and security and to \nincrease police patrolling in areas where sizeable African community resides. \nIt has al so been decided to hold regular meetings with the African community \nin all major metropolitan cities.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |631", "t": "IT Companies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 631 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 20.07.2016 \n \n \nIT COMPANIES \n \n631.  DR. K. KAMARAJ: \n \nWill the Minister of Electronics & Information technology be pleased to state: - \n \n(a) the number of registered Information Technology (IT) companies functioning in  the \ncountry as on date, State-wise; \n(b) whether more than 50% of the companies working in the field of IT sector are not \nregistered; \n(c) if so, the reaction of the Government thereto; \n(d) whether revenue loss as a result thereof to the exchequer has been assessed; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n  \n \n(a): As per the Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA),  Government of India, the number of \nregistered IT Companies functioning in the country as on 30.06.2016 is 95,084.  The State/UT \nwise list of Registered IT Companies is given in Annexure.     \n \n(b): As per the  MCA, information of companies working in the field of IT sector not registered \nwith Registrar of Companies is not maintained.  \n \n(c) to (e): Do not arise. \n******* \n \n  \n\n  \nAnnexure \n \nState/UT-wise number of Active IT Companies in India as on 30.06.2016 \nSl. No. State Number \n1 A&N Islands 4 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 4,250 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 3 \n4 Assam 189 \n5 Bihar 764 \n6 Chandigarh 846 \n7 Chhattisgarh 278 \n8 Daman and Diu 4 \n9 Delhi 16,427 \n10 Dadar Nagar Haveli 5 \n11 Goa 170 \n12 Gujarat 3,616 \n13 Himachal Pradesh 173 \n14 Haryana 2,249 \n15 Jharkhand 392 \n16 Jammu and Kashmir 245 \n17 Karnataka 13,117 \n18 Kerala 3,439 \n19 Lakshadweep - \n20 Maharashtra 14,949 \n21 Meghalaya 16 \n22 Manipur 22 \n23 Madhya Pradesh 1,681 \n24 Mizoram 2 \n25 Nagaland 8 \n26 Orissa 1,007 \n27 Punjab 828 \n28 Pondicherry 143 \n29 Rajasthan 2,264 \n30 Sikkim - \n31 Telangana 10,285 \n32 Tamil Nadu 9,416 \n33 Tripura 25 \n34 Uttar Pradesh 3,806 \n35 Uttarakhand 292 \n36 West Bengal 4,169 \nTotal 95,084 \nNote:  IT Companies are those having First three digits of Activity Code (NIC-2004) amongst \n\n(721,722,723,724,725 and 729) \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |632", "t": "Conversion of Railway Stations", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.632 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCONVERSION OF RAILWAY STATIONS \n \n632.  ADV. NARENDRA KESHAV SAWAIKAR: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n      \n(a) whether the Railways has identified a few railway stations for \nconversion into world class stations; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the criteria for selection \nof these stations; and \n \n(c) whether the Railways intends to rope in corporations with \nNon-Governmental Organizations (NGOs) and Non -Resident \nIndians (NRIs) in the programme in view of financial crunch and \nif so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n**** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFE RRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  632 BY ADV. NARENDRA KESHAV \nSAWAIKAR TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 \nREGARDING CONVERSION OF RAILWAY STATIONS. \n(a)&(b): Indian Railway has advertised its plan to redevelop ‘A-1’ and \n‘A’ category stations (about 400 in number)  which are generally \nlocated in metros, major cities, pilgrimage centres and important \ntourist destinations on ‘as is where is’ basis, by inviting proposals \nfrom interested parties with their designs and business ideas. The \nentire cost of station redevelopment is to be met by leveraging \ncommercial development  of land and air space in and around the \nstations.   \n(c)  Railways have issued guidelines for provision, augmentation and \nimprovement of passenger amenities at railway stations through \nindividuals, NGOs, Trusts, Charitable Institutions, Corporations etc.  \nThese guidelines have also been sent to High Commission/Embassy \nof United States of America, United Kingdom, Canada and Australia \nwith a view to elicit cooperation from Non -Resident Indians (NRIs) \nin this regard. \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |633", "t": "Capacity Building in IT", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 633 \n                                         TO BE ANSWERED ON: 20.07.2016 \n \nCAPACITY BUILDING IN  IT \n  \n633.  SHRI RAMESH BIDHURI: \n \nWill the Minister of Electronics and Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n(a)     whether the Government has made a road -map for capacity building in the field of rural \nIT infrastructure;   \n(b)      if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the steps taken to strengthen the digital education in rural areas particularly among the \nrural youths? \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a) to (c) :  Yes, Sir. The Government of India has undertaken following initiatives for capacity \nbuilding in field of rural IT infrastructure: \n \ni)  National Optical Fibre Network (NOFN):  The Government  has approved, ' National \nOptical Fibre Network (NOFN)/BharatNet' , to establish network infrastructure to connect all the \nGram Panchayats (2.5 lakh) in the country by laying incremental fibre to bridge the connectivity \ngap between Gram Panchayats and Blocks or through radio/satellite for providing broadband  \nconnectivity. It is being implemented through a Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV), Bharat \nBroadband Network Limited (BBNL).  Till June,2016 more than 50,465 Gram Panchayats (GPs) \nhave been connected with OFC.  \n \nii)  Under Digital India programme, the Government ha s launched CSC 2.0 Scheme to set up \nat least one Common Service Centre (CSC) to cover all the 2.5 lakh Gram Panchayats of the \nCountry for delivery of various electronic services to citizens across rural India. This would \ninclude strengthening and integrating the existing 100,000 CSCs under the original CSC scheme \nand making operational an additional 1.5 lakh CSCs in Gram Panchayats. The Project is to be \nimplemented over a period of 4 years. Till June,2016   a total number of  1,22,793 CSCs have \nbeen rolled out at Gram Panchayat level.  \n \niii)  The Government is implementing following schemes  for providing digital education and \nliteracy to the masses (including rural India): \n \n\n(a) Department of  Electronics & Information Technology ( DeitY) is implementing a \nproject viz; “Course on Computer Education in Rural India” for Training and Certification \nof one lakh Common Service Centre (CSC) Operators/ Village Level Entrepreneurs (VLE) \nin every state of the country with financial support of Rs. 750.00 lakh  through National \nInstitute of Electronics and Information Technology (NIELIT), an autonomous society \nunder DeitY . Under this project, a total of 1,00,000 VLEs are targeted for Course on \nComputer Concepts (CCC) by March, 2017.   \n \n \n \n(b) DeitY is implementing a project viz; “ Empowering Women in Rural India through \nDigital Literacy (WDLP) with an outlay of  Rs. 287.50 lakh through NIELIT, with an aim \nat training and empowering 25,000 rural  women. The training and examination of 25,000 \nwomen has been completed.   \n \n(c)  National Digital Literacy Mission (NDLM)  scheme was approved in March 2014 with \nan aim to train 10 lakh person with a total budget outlay of Rs. 97.02 crore. \n  \n(d)  Digital Empowerment of citizens by providing Universal Digital Literacy is an \nintegral component of the vision of 'Digital India' initiative. Keeping this in view, a scheme \nentitled 'Digital Saksharta Abhiyan' (DISHA) to make 42.5 lakh persons digitally literate in \nselected households throughout the country was approved in December 2014.  \n \nBoth the above schemes on digital literacy  are being implemented concurrently  and so far \naround 72.92 lakh candidates have been trained and approximately 33.15 lakh candidates \nhave been certified. A total of 1952 training partners are involved under these schemes. Out \nof these Training Partners/ Training Centres, around 57% exist in rural areas (including \nnearly 30,000 CSCs).  \n \n(e) A scheme to make 6 crore rural households digitally literate has also been drawn up in the \ncurrent financial year. \n \niv) A scheme for setting up/upgrading of  NIELIT centres is also under implementation to \ncover rural and remote parts of the country in J&K and North East (NE). The Scheme entails \nsetting up of 10 new extension centres and upgradation of 8 existing centres in NE. One \nextension centre in Leh district of J&K has also been setup. \n \n******** \n  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |634", "t": "Increase in Frequency", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 634 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINCREASE IN FREQUENCY \n \n†634. SHRI RAJESH VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to operate train no. 14611 -\n14612 up -down daily and attach sleeper and air conditioned \ncoaches keeping public welfare in mind;  \n \n(b) if so, the time by which train no. 14611 -14612 up-down will run \nwith sleeper and air conditioned coaches; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a) to (c)  14611/14612 Amritsar -Gorakhpur Express (weekly) is \npresently running in integrated rake link with fully unreserved \n14603/14604 Amritsar -Saharsa Jan Sadharan Express (weekly) \nmeant for General Class passengers.   Hence, increase in frequency \nof 14611/14612 Amritsar -Gorakhpur Express (weekly) from weekly \nto daily is not feasible due to operational and resource constraints.  \nFurther, 14611/14612 Amritsar-Gorakhpur Express (weekly) is a fully \nun-reserved train service.  As such, attachment of AC and Sleeper \nclass coaches in this train is operationally not feasible, as it will \nchange the very character of such train. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |635", "t": "NSSO Data on Creation of Jobs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 635 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 20TH JULY, 2016 \n \nNSSO DATA ON CREATION OF JOBS \n \n635. SHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL: \n \nWill the Minister of STATISTI CS AND PROGRAMME \nIMPLEMENTATION be pleased to state  the number of jobs  created \nduring each of the last three years  and the current year as per the \nlatest data of the National Sample Survey Organisation (NSSO), sector-\nwise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n[SHRI D.V. SADANANDA GOWDA] \n \nLast survey of National Sample Survey Office (NSSO) on Employment -\nUnemployment was conducted during July, 2011 – June, 2012 (68 th \nround of NSS). However, t o assess the effect of economic slowdown \non employment in India , Labour Bureau, Ministry of Labour & \nEmployment, has been conducting Quarterly Quick Employment \nsurveys in selected labour -intensive and export -oriented sectors , \nnamely, textiles including apparels, leather, metals, automobiles, \ngems & jewellery, transport, IT/BPO and handloom/powerloom. Based \non the latest available results from these surveys , the estimated net \naddition of jobs during each of the last three years  is given at \nAnnexure.  \n\nAnnexure \nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. \n635 for 20.7.2016 \n***** \n \n***** \n \nSector wise estimated net addition in employment \n(in Lakhs) \nSl. \nNo Industry/ Group \nJanuary \n2013 – \nDecember \n2013 \nJanuary \n2014 – \nDecember \n2014 \nJanuary \n2015 – \nDecember \n2015 \n1 Textiles 2.86 1.41 0.72 \n2 Leather 0.44 -0.07 -0.08 \n3 Metal -0.35 0.74 0.37 \n4 Automobile 0.16 0.25 -0.08 \n5 Gems & Jewellery 0.09 0.11 -0.19 \n6 Transport -0.09 -0.11 -0.04 \n7 IT/BPO 1.09 1.93 0.76 \n8 Handloom/ Powerloom -0.02 -0.05 -0.11 \n Total 4.19 4.21 1.35 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |636", "t": "Demand and Supply of Uranium", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 636 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nDEMAND AND SUPPLY OF URANIUM \n \n636.  SHRI S.P.MUDDAHANUME GOWDA: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether there is a gap between demand and supp ly of uranium for the \n nuclear power plants of the country; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons the refor; \n \n(c)  the measures taken to meet the demand of urani um for smooth functioning \n of nuclear projects; and \n \n(d)  the extent to which these steps have been succ essful? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR, PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVA NCES AND \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER'S OFFICE (DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) & (b) No, Sir.   There are currently twenty one  (21) reactors with an installed \ncapacity of 5780 MW.   Of these, thirteen (13) reac tors with a capacity of \n3380 MW are under IAEA Safeguards and use imported uranium which \nis available in adequate quantity.  Eight (8) react ors with aggregate \ncapacity of 2400 MW are fuelled by indigenous urani um.  These reactors \nare now being operated close to their rated capacit y. In addition, one unit \n(Kudankulam Unit-2) has also attained first critica lity (start of controlled \nself-sustaining nuclear fission chain reaction in t he Reactor for the first \ntime) on July 10, 2016.  This unit also uses imported fuel.  \n  \n(c)  The Government has taken measures to augment d omestic uranium \nsupply by opening of new mines and processing facil ities and importing \nfuel for reactors under IAEA Safeguards. \n \n(d)    The steps have resulted in operation of nuclear po wer reactors at or \nclose to their rated capacity. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |637", "t": "Strength of Bureaucrats", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF PERSONNEL & TRAINING) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 637 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016) \n \nSTRENGTH OF BUREAUCRATS \n \n637. SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA: \n        SHRI PR. SENTHIL NATHAN: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has taken  any decision on the cadre sanctioned  \nstrength of IAS and IPS officers in the country, State-wise; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the  recruitments made during the last three  years, \nyear-wise and cadre-wise; \n(c)  the steps taken by the Government  to direct State Governments to fill up  \nadequate IAS and IPS officers in their  respective States from their  State \nGovernment Services in the coming years; and  \n(d)  the total expenditure incurred by  the central exchequer for the overall  \nexpenditure of IAS and IPS officers in the country, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions \nand Minister of State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a) &  (b): The Sanctioned strength of the India Administrative Service (IAS) and \nIndian Police Service  (IPS) officers of any given cadre is reviewed ordinarily at the \ninterval of every five years. Cadre-wise details of officers allocated to IAS and IPS on \nthe basis of Civil Services Examination - 2012 to 2014 are at Annexure -I and \nAnnexure-II respectively.  \n \n(c): The appointment by promotion to IAS/IPS from State Civil Service/ State \nPolice Service is governed by the statutory provisions, which envisage separate role to \nCentral Government, State Governments and Union Public Service Commission \n(UPSC). The vac ancies to be filled up are determined year wise and selection \ncommittee meetings are conducted by the UPSC for preparation of select list on \nreceipt of the proposals from the State Governments/UTs. Periodic meetings are \nconducted by the UPSC and Central Go vernment with the State Governments to \nexpedite the proposals for the Selection Committee Meetings so that the vacancies are \nfilled up expeditiously. \n \n(d): The information regarding total expenditure incurred by the central exchequer \nfor the overall  expenditure of IAS and IPS officers in the country, State -wise is not \nmaintained. \n******** \n\nANNEXURE-I \n \nAnnexure-I mentioned in reply to part (a)& (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 637asked by SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA and SHRI PR. \nSENTHIL NATHAN to be replied on 20.07.201 6  regarding “Strength of \nBureaucrats” \n \nAllocation of IAS (Direct Recruit) officer to various cadres during last 3 years  \n \nSr. No. Name of Cadre CSE- 2012 CSE- 2013 CSE-2014 \n1. A G M U T 12 11 11 \n2. Andhra Pradesh 10* 10* 5 \n3. Assam Meghalaya 7 7 8 \n4. Bihar 10 9 10 \n5. Chhattisgarh 7 7 5 \n6. Gujarat 7 10 9 \n7. Haryana 4 5 4 \n8. Himachal Pradesh 5 4 4 \n9. Jammu & Kashmir 4 4 4 \n10. Jharkhand 7 7 7 \n11. Karnataka 8 8 9 \n12. Kerala 6 6 6 \n13. Madhya Pradesh 13 13 13 \n14. Maharashtra 8 9 8 \n15. Manipur 6* 6* 3 \n16. Nagaland 4 4 4 \n17. Orissa 6 6 7 \n18. Punjab 6 6 5 \n19. Rajasthan 8 8 8 \n20. Sikkim 1 1 1 \n21. Tamil Nadu 9 9 10 \n22. Telangana  *  * 4 \n23. Tripura *   * 3 \n24. Uttar Pradesh 17 17 19 \n25. Uttarakhand 3 3 3 \n26. West Bengal 12 10 10 \nTotal   180 180 180 \n* For CSE -2012 and CSE -2013 cadre allocation was made to erstwhile cadre of \nAndhra Pradesh and Joint Cadre of Manipur-Tripura. \n  \n\nANNEXURE-II \n \nAnnexure-II mentioned in reply to part (a)& (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 637asked by SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA and SHRI PR. \nSENTHIL NATHAN to be replied on 20.07.201 6  regarding “Strength of \nBureaucrats” \n \nAllocation of IPS (Direct Recruit) officer to various cadres during last 3 years  \n \nSl. No. Name of Cadre CSE- 2012 CSE- 2013 CSE- 2014 \n01. Andhra Pradesh 07* 04 05 \n02. AGMUT 11 10 08 \n03. Assam-Meghalaya 07 07 06 \n04. Bihar 07 07 05 \n05. Chhattisgarh 04 04 01 \n06. Gujarat 07 06 05 \n07. Haryana 04 05 04 \n08. Himachal Pradesh 03 03 03 \n09. Jammu & Kashmir 04 04 03 \n10. Jharkhand 05 04 05 \n11. Karnataka 06 06 07 \n12. Kerala 04 05 06 \n13. Madhya Pradesh 10 09 09 \n14. Maharashtra 09 09 11 \n15. Manipur 06* 04 07 \n16. Nagaland 04 03 04 \n17. Odisha 05 06 04 \n18. Punjab 05 05 05 \n19. Rajasthan 05 05 04 \n20. Sikkim 0 01 01 \n21. Tamil Nadu 08 07 06 \n22. Telangana  * 03 02 \n23. Tripura * 02 02 \n24. Uttar Pradesh 17 19 21 \n25. Uttarakhand  02 02 01 \n26. West Bengal 10 10 15 \n Total 150 150 150 \n     * For CSE-2012 cadre allocation was made to erstwhile cadre of Andhra Pradesh    \nand Joint Cadre of Manipur-Tripura. \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |638", "t": "Welfare of Minorities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.638 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nWelfare of Minorities \n \n \n    638.  KUMARI SHOBHA KARANDLAJE: \n \n Will the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the amount spent on the welfare of minorities in various States including in the State of \nKarnataka during each of the last three years and the current year under the Multi -\nSectoral Developmen t Programme, Educational Schemes, Seekho  Aur Kamao (Learn \nand Earn), Nai  Roshni, ( Leadership Development of Minority Women), National \nMinorities Development and Finance Corporation (NMDFC); and \n(b)  the  amount likely to be spent under Pre -Matric Scholarship Scheme, Merit-cum-Means \nBased Scholarship Scheme and Free Coaching and Allied Schem e in variousStates \nincluding the State of Karnataka during the above period?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF MINISTRY OF MINORITY \nAFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a) and (b) Funds released to the Project Implementing Agencies/NGOs/S tate \nChannelising Agencies (SCAs) for implementation of (i) Seekho aur Kamao (Learn and \nEarn) (ii) Nai Roshni – Leadership Development of Minority Women (iii) National \nMinorities Development and Finance Corporation (NMDFC) in various states including \nKarnataka during last three years and current year may please be seen  at Annexure -I, \nAnnexure-II and Annexure-III respectively. \nThe State/UT wise statement of funds released under the Scheme of Multi Sectoral \nDevelopment Programme is at Annexure-IV.  \nThe State /UT -wise details of funds released under the Pre-matric Scholarship \nScheme,  Post-matric Scholarship Scheme  may please be seen at Annexure V. The \nState/UT -wise details of funds released under the Merit-cum-Means based Scholarship \nScheme may please be seen at Annexure –VI.  \n \n \n \n\n \nUnder the scheme of Maulana Azad National Fellowship, there is neither any state -\nwise fund allocation nor is there any state-wise fund release. \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released under the Free Coaching and Allied \nScheme may please be seen at Annexure VII. The State/UT -wise details of funds \nreleased under the schemes of Support to minority candidates clearing Prelims \nconducted by UPSC/SSC, State Public Service Commission (PSC) etc. Padho \nPardesh- Interest Subsidy on Educati onal Loans for overseas studies  Jiyo Parsi \nmay please be seen at Annexure VIII respectively. \nNai Manzil - The Nai Manzil scheme has been approved with the cost of Rs. 650.00 \ncrore for five years. 50% funding has to come from the World Bank. The World Bank \nhas approved the funding of US$ 50 million. Rs. 155.00 crore has been earmarked for \n2016-17 for implementation of programme.  \n***** \n  \n\n ANNEXURE-I   \nLok Sabha Unstarred Question No.638  raised by Kumari Sobha Karandlaje regarding \nWelfare of Minorities to be answered on 20.07.2016  \n \n  \nFunds 